Full audit — five things, one rewrite:
1. your ask: `target="_blank"` to open in a new tab;
2. the security catch that comes with #1: `target="_blank"` without `rel="noopener noreferrer"` lets the opened page access `window.opener` — a known vulnerability, always pair the two;
3. no layout at all → flex row with gap;
4. muted color with hover to full color (standard link treatment for icon/text row navigation, not underlined body-text style);
5. no dark mode;
Also added `aria-label` per link since a future icon-only version would need it — cheap to add now, matches the pattern used elsewhere in the project.
Writing it:
<tool_call>
{"name": "write_file", "arguments": {"path": "components/SocialLinks.tsx", "content": "export default function SocialLinks() {
  const links = [
    { label: "Twitter", href: "https://twitter.com/example" },
    { label: "GitHub", href: "https://github.com/example" },
  ];
  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
      {links.map((link) => (
        <a
          key={link.label}
          href={link.href}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          aria-label={link.label}
          className="text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-400 dark:hover:text-zinc-100"
        >
          {link.label}
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
"}}
</tool_call>

